<title>USA: Oil majors pursue LatAm, keeping eye on the future.</title>
<headline>Oil majors pursue LatAm, keeping eye on the future.</headline>
<byline>Patrick Connole</byline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil majors are more willing than ever to spend billions of dollars exploring, developing and transporting Latin American energy reserves, claiming the time has come to aggressively pursue new opportunities.</p>
<p>What drives the majors is a continent of 320 million people, experiencing a return to economic growth -- 3.7 pct in 1994 -- lower inflation and a tide of will to open markets.</p>
</text>
